cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Vantyx in research, teaching, or a language survey, cite this repository."
title: "Vantyx: a gradual-typing language with an interpreter, a native C11 backend, and a dependency-free AI host"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zeidex"
    alias: "zeiad6"
    website: "https://zeidexlink.zeidexsoft.com/zeidex"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zeiad6/vantyx"
abstract: >-
  Vantyx is a pre-1.0 programming language with Python-like syntax, optional
  type annotations, a tree-walking reference interpreter, a native GNU C11
  backend for a statically typed subset, and a dependency-free AI host toolkit.
  The interpreter is the semantic oracle; native behavior is checked by
  differential tests. The AI host covers providers, structured extraction,
  embeddings, local retrieval with citations, tools, and bounded agents.
keywords:
  - programming language
  - gradual typing
  - interpreter
  - compiler
  - C11
  - Rust
  - AI tooling
